stocks\n        Task Inputs: [{\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"procedural\": \"check requirements, apply, verify, submit details\", \"policy\": \"eligibility criteria, age requirement, income limits, qualifying conditions\", \"conceptual\": \"credit card eligibility, applicant requirements, bank policy\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"Credit_Card\", \"target_intent\": [\"Eligibility\"]}, \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_b3c9ded6\", \"content\": \"Question: What are the requirements for applying for a Horizon Bank credit card?\\n\\nAnswer: To be considered for a Horizon Bank credit card, you must meet specific criteria. If you are a Singaporean citizen or permanent resident between the ages of {{faq_b3c9ded6_001}} and {{faq_b3c9ded6_002}}, you will need to have an annual income of at least {{faq_b3c9ded6_003}}. For foreigners with a valid work pass, the requirement is an annual income of {{faq_b3c9ded6_004}}. Alternatively, if you are above {{faq_b3c9ded6_005}} years old, the annual income requirements are {{faq_b3c9ded6_006}} for Singaporean citizens or permanent residents, and {{faq_b3c9ded6_007}} for foreigners with a valid work pass.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_dcf718fa\", \"content\": \"Question: Am I qualified to apply for a Horizon Bank credit card?\\n\\nAnswer: - Applicants aged {{faq_dcf718fa_001}} to {{faq_dcf718fa_002}} may submit a credit‑card request if they meet one of the following income criteria:\\n  • Singapore citizen or permanent resident: minimum annual earnings of {{faq_dcf718fa_003}}.\\n  • Foreign national holding a valid work pass: minimum annual earnings of {{faq_dcf718fa_004}}.\\n- Applicants older than {{faq_dcf718fa_005}} are also eligible provided they satisfy one of these conditions:\\n  • Singapore citizen or permanent resident: minimum annual earnings of {{faq_dcf718fa_006}}.\\n  • Foreign national holding a valid work pass: minimum annual earnings of {{faq_dcf718fa_007}}.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_c241b12d\", \"content\": \"Question: As a senior citizen, am I eligible to apply for a Horizon Bank credit card, and what are the key requirements I need to fulfill?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, we welcome applications from retirees who meet specific criteria. To qualify for our credit card with a credit limit of {{faq_c241b12d_001}}, you must be a Singapore citizen or permanent resident, aged {{faq_c241b12d_002}} or above, have an assessed annual income of less than {{faq_c241b12d_003}}, and not hold any existing credit cards or unsecured loans with us. If you meet these conditions, you may be eligible for our credit card, subject to our standard banking requirements.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_c844d766\", \"content\": \"Question: As a retired individual, what documentation do I need to provide to verify my income when applying for a Horizon Bank credit card or requesting a credit limit increase?\\n\\nAnswer: To proceed with your application, please identify yourself as a retiree and, if you are {{faq_c844d766_001}} or older, be prepared to upload your CPF LIFE payout transaction records from the past two months. You can access these records through the my CPF portal by navigating to My dashboards, then Retirement, followed by Monthly payouts, and finally Monthly payout history. Ensure you have the latest version of the Horizon App installed to facilitate a seamless application process.\"}]}, {\"task_id\": \"task_2\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_2\", \"procedural\": \"calculate fees, pay charges, trade stocks, buy securities\", \"policy\": \"brokerage fee structure, trading costs, commission charges, pricing limits\", \"conceptual\": \"stock trading fees, investment costs, transaction charges\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"Stocks\", \"target_intent\": [\"Fees And Charges\"]}, \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_b8e22edc\", \"content\": \"Question: How does Horizon Bank's fee structure work for investment transactions?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, we provide a competitive fee environment for our investors. Until December {{faq_b8e22edc_001}}, {{faq_b8e22edc_002}}, trading US stocks and ETFs is commission-free. After this period, a commission of {{faq_b8e22edc_003}} applies, with a minimum charge of USD {{faq_b8e22edc_004}} per trade. For UK UCITS ETFs, a commission rate of {{faq_b8e22edc_005}} is applicable, with a minimum fee of USD {{faq_b8e22edc_006}} per trade. Additionally, a {{faq_b8e22edc_007}} GST is levied on commissions, and your Trade Confirmation will also serve as your Tax Invoice. Notably, Horizon Bank does not impose platform, custody, settlement, or corporate action handling fees. For a detailed breakdown, please navigate to the Horizon App, select your Profile, and then access the Legal section to view the Stocks Fee Schedule.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_91bd0060\", \"content\": \"Question: Can you provide information on the characteristics of UCITS ETFs listed in the UK and their tax implications for international investors?\\n\\nAnswer: Horizon Bank offers access to European-regulated exchange-traded funds, known as UCITS ETFs, which are traded on the London Stock Exchange. These funds are designed to enhance risk management and diversification strategies. Notably, Irish-domiciled UCITS ETFs are subject to a reduced withholding tax of {{faq_91bd0060_001}} on dividends for certain investors, such as those residing in Singapore, compared to the {{faq_91bd0060_002}} withholding tax applicable to US ETFs. Please note that this information is for general purposes only and should not be considered as tax, legal, or financial guidance. It's also worth noting that the base currency for trading UK UCITS ETFs through Horizon Bank is the US Dollar (USD).\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_b73dbebe\", \"content\": \"Question: Does Horizon Bank offer personalized investment guidance to its clients?\\n\\nAnswer: Horizon Bank maintains a neutral stance and does not extend investment advice to its customers, allowing them to make independent decisions regarding their financial portfolios.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_1751281e\", \"content\": \"Question: What distinguishes American and British exchange-traded funds within the Horizon App's search functionality?\\n\\nAnswer: To discern between US and UK-based exchange-traded funds, simply look for the respective 'US' or 'UK' designation that accompanies each fund's ticker symbol when conducting a search on the Horizon App.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Return one result for every supplied task_id.\n        - For SUFFICIENT, return only parent IDs from that exact task that are directly relevant. At least one approved ID is required.\n        - For RETRY, return no approved IDs and concise query-refinement feedback. The backend determines terminal UNAVAILABLE status after three failed attempts.\n        - Treat {placeholders} in parent content as valid approved facts.\n        - Never invent a parent ID, fact, or instruction.\n\n        Output JSON only: {\"task_results\": [{\"task_id\": \"...\", \"status\": \"SUFFICIENT\" | \"RETRY\" | \"UNAVAILABLE\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [\"...\"], \"reason\": \"...\", \"search_feedback\": \"...\"}]}\n        "}
