id work pass in the same age range need an annual income of S$60,000.\n- Applicants older than 55 years are also eligible if they meet the higher income thresholds: S$15,000 for Singapore citizens/PRs and S$60,000 for foreigners with a work pass.\n- For seniors, the bank offers a credit‑card with a limit of S$500 to Singapore citizens or PRs aged 56 or above, provided their assessed annual income is below S$15,000 and they hold no other Horizon credit cards or unsecured loans.\n- Retirees must identify themselves as such and, if they are 65 or older, upload CPF LIFE payout transaction records from the past two months as income verification.\n\n**Stock trading fees**\n- Trading US stocks and ETFs is commission‑free until December 31 2026. After that date a commission of 0.05% applies, with a minimum charge of USD 2.99 per trade.\n- For UK UCITS ETFs the commission rate is 0.05% with a minimum fee of USD 4 per trade.\n- A 9% GST is added to all commissions.\n- Horizon Bank does not charge platform, custody, settlement, or corporate‑action handling fees. For a full breakdown, view the Stocks Fee Schedule in the Horizon App under Profile → Legal.\nUser: what's the eligibility of credit card\n    User Baseline (advisory only; do not treat it as a current request): None\n    Latest User Input: \"what's the eligibility of credit card\"\n    \n    TRIAGE A BANKING REQUEST.\n    1. ESCALATION: User explicitly demands a human agent or manager.\n    2. CLARIFICATION: The input is PURELY chitchat, greetings, or completely unrelated to banking (e.g., \"Hello\", \"How are you\", \"What is the weather\"). \n    3. VALID_REQUEST: A banking question, follow-up, or request that can be answered from Horizon FAQ knowledge.\n    \n    Output JSON ONLY:\n    {\"triage_status\": \"ESCALATION\" | \"CLARIFICATION\" | \"VALID_REQUEST\"}\n    "}
