{"timestamp": "2026-08-16T02:42:55.010+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_dfabab3d-f380-4022-8da7-4dac0ea9b0c6", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n        TASK-LEVEL SUFFICIENCY AND EVIDENCE SELECTION\n        You are a groundedness auditor for a read-only Horizon Bank FAQ assistant.\n        Evaluate EACH supplied task independently. A parent is sufficient only if it directly supports that task.\n\n        User Request: How do I open an account, I lost my credit card, and how can I start buying stocks?\n        Trusted Conversation Context: Long-Term Conversation Context (advisory only):\nCredit card eligibility: Singapore citizens/PRs 21‑55 need ≥S$30k annual income; >55 need ≥S$15k. Foreign nationals with work pass 21‑55 need ≥S$60k; >55 also ≥S$60k. Applications require Singapore residency, SingPass/MyInfo via Horizon app; processing up to 5 business days. To open an account, launch Horizon app and log in with SingPass. For a lost card, use the app’s card dashboard to freeze the card and order a replacement.\n\nCurrent Session (latest 10 turns):\nAI: Welcome back. Last time I explained the credit card eligibility criteria and how to freeze a lost card using the Horizon app; would you like to continue that discussion or explore something else?\nUser: How do I open an account, I lost my credit card, and how can I start buying stocks?\n        Task Inputs: [{\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"procedural\": \"Horizon app, open account, login, SingPass\", \"policy\": \"account creation rules, requirements\", \"conceptual\": \"deposit account, Horizon Bank\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"Deposit_Account\", \"target_intent\": [\"Application\", \"Account Management\"]}, \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_70aebcd6\", \"content\": \"Question: What information and tools are necessary to open a Savings Account with Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: - A mobile phone together with MyInfo verification to auto‑populate your application form.\\n- If you delete or reinstall the Horizon App after successfully registering, you will still need to authenticate via SingPass when you log in again.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_b9f2a2b9\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the youngest age at which a person can open a Savings Account with Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: - Minimum age: {{faq_b9f2a2b9_001}} years old or older.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_46c43248\", \"content\": \"Question: Can I open a Savings Account with Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: - You are eligible to apply for a Horizon Bank Savings Account if you meet both of the following criteria:\\n  {{faq_46c43248_001}}. You are a Singapore citizen, a Singapore permanent resident, or a foreign national holding a valid work pass.\\n  {{faq_46c43248_002}}. You are {{faq_46c43248_003}} years of age or older.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_5123ef30\", \"content\": \"Question: What steps must I take to reactivate my Horizon savings account?\\n\\nAnswer: - To restore access to your Horizon savings account, use the Horizon App and follow these steps:\\n{{faq_5123ef30_001}}. Sign in to the Horizon App.\\n{{faq_5123ef30_002}}. Choose the Singpass QR‑code option and authenticate via the Singpass mobile app.\\n{{faq_5123ef30_003}}. Once verification is complete, set up a new six‑digit passcode for future logins.\"}]}, {\"task_id\": \"task_2\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_2\", \"procedural\": \"Horizon app, freeze card, report lost, order replacement\", \"policy\": \"card security, replacement procedure\", \"conceptual\": \"lost credit card, card dashboard\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"Credit_Card\", \"target_intent\": [\"Card Logistics\", \"Authentication And Security\"]}, \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_7883a8c2\", \"content\": \"Question: My Horizon card is missing—what steps should I take?\\n\\nAnswer: - If you cannot locate your Horizon card, you can temporarily freeze it through the Horizon App:\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_001}}. Sign in to the Horizon App.\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_002}}. On the card overview screen, tap \\\"View & Manage Card.\\\"\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_003}}. Select \\\"Freeze Card.\\\"\\n- For a card that is lost or stolen, first freeze it and then request a replacement:\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_004}}. Log into the Horizon App.\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_005}}. Open the card dashboard and choose \\\"View & Manage Card.\\\"\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_006}}. Tap \\\"Freeze Card\\\" followed by \\\"Order Replacement.\\\"\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_007}}. Horizon will issue a new card and permanently deactivate the old one.\\n- You may also wish to file a police report.\\n- The new card will arrive with a different card number; be sure to update any recurring payments (e.g., subscriptions) with the new details.\\n- For additional assistance, select \\\"Contact Us\\\" from the app menu.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_33f045af\", \"content\": \"Question: My Horizon card has been compromised due to physical damage. What steps should I take to obtain a new one from Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: To acquire a replacement card, follow these straightforward steps: \\n    * Access your Horizon App account \\n    * Navigate to the 'Card Management' section \\n    * Choose the 'Replace Current Card' option \\n    * Indicate that your card is damaged to complete the request\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_74392fe2\", \"content\": \"Question: I've applied for a new Horizon card, but it hasn't arrived yet. What steps can I take to resolve the issue?\\n\\nAnswer: To address the non-receipt of your replacement Horizon card, please get in touch with our dedicated support team through the following channels: \\n    * Utilize the live chat feature or initiate a voice call directly from your Horizon App \\n    * Alternatively, you can reach us by dialing +{{faq_74392fe2_001}} {{faq_74392fe2_002}}-HORIZON\"}]}, {\"task_id\": \"task_3\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_3\", \"procedural\": \"buy stocks, invest, trading setup\", \"policy\": \"trading rules, eligibility\", \"conceptual\": \"stocks, wealth management\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"Stocks\", \"target_intent\": [\"Wealth And Insurance\", \"General Inquiries\"]}, \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_502da680\", \"content\": \"Question: What are the initial steps to begin buying and selling securities with Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: To initiate trading activities, it is necessary to establish a securities trading account. This can be accomplished by navigating to the Horizon App, selecting the Investments option, and then choosing the Stocks feature. Upon doing so, adhere to the on-screen prompts to finalize the account setup. Please be aware that the approval to open this account is contingent upon an internal evaluation conducted by Horizon Bank.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_4bd34aa4\", \"content\": \"Question: At Horizon Bank, what is the lowest investment threshold for purchasing securities?\\n\\nAnswer: With Horizon Bank, you have the flexibility to initiate your investment portfolio by buying stocks and ETFs with a minimum investment of just USD {{faq_4bd34aa4_001}}.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_c8d61dc6\", \"content\": \"Question: What investment opportunities are available through Horizon Bank's stock trading services?\\n\\nAnswer: Horizon Bank provides its clients with the ability to engage in trading activities involving stocks and exchange-traded funds listed on US exchanges, in addition to a selection of UK UCITS exchange-traded funds.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_e94ad933\", \"content\": \"Question: What are the eligibility criteria for creating a Stocks account with Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: To be eligible for a Stocks account, you must meet the following conditions: \\n      * You should have an active Savings account with Horizon Bank. If you haven't already, you can easily open one through the Horizon App.\\n      * Your age should be between {{faq_e94ad933_001}} and {{faq_e94ad933_002}} years. Additionally, please be aware that individuals classified as US persons are not eligible to open a Stocks account with Horizon Bank.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Return one result for every supplied task_id.\n        - For SUFFICIENT, return only parent IDs from that exact task that are directly relevant. At least one approved ID is required.\n        - For RETRY, return no approved IDs and concise query-refinement feedback. The backend determines terminal UNAVAILABLE status after three failed attempts.\n        - Treat {placeholders} in parent content as valid approved facts.\n        - Never invent a parent ID, fact, or instruction.\n\n        Output JSON only: {\"task_results\": [{\"task_id\": \"...\", \"status\": \"SUFFICIENT\" | \"RETRY\" | \"UNAVAILABLE\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [\"...\"], \"reason\": \"...\", \"search_feedback\": \"...\"}]}\n        "}
