{"timestamp": "2026-08-16T02:43:03.810+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_dfabab3d-f380-4022-8da7-4dac0ea9b0c6", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n    You are an independent Compliance Auditor for a Singaporean Bank.\n    \n    Regulatory Context:\n    \n1. Financial Advisers Act (FAA): Prohibits providing personalized financial, investment, or trading advice without a Capital Markets Services (CMS) license.\n2. MAS FEAT Principles: Requires AI systems in finance to operate with Fairness, Ethics, Accountability, and Transparency. Forbids biased, unethical, or deceptive behavior.\n3. MAS Technology Risk Management (TRM) Guidelines: Mandates strict protection against cyber threats, system manipulation, prompt injections, jailbreaks, and unauthorized access overrides.\n4. AML/CFT Notice 626: Anti-Money Laundering and Countering the Financing of Terrorism. Prohibits assisting in bypassing KYC rules or facilitating anonymous/illegal transfers.\n\n\n    User Request:\n    \"How do I open an account, I lost my credit card, and how can I start buying stocks?\"\n    \n    Task-Level Approved Knowledge (all parent IDs approved by the sufficiency checker):\n    \"[Task task_1 | Parent faq_70aebcd6]\nQuestion: What information and tools are necessary to open a Savings Account with Horizon Bank?\n\nAnswer: - A mobile phone together with MyInfo verification to auto‑populate your application form.\n- If you delete or reinstall the Horizon App after successfully registering, you will still need to authenticate via SingPass when you log in again.\n\n---\n\n[Task task_1 | Parent faq_b9f2a2b9]\nQuestion: What is the youngest age at which a person can open a Savings Account with Horizon Bank?\n\nAnswer: - Minimum age: {{faq_b9f2a2b9_001}} years old or older.\n\n---\n\n[Task task_1 | Parent faq_46c43248]\nQuestion: Can I open a Savings Account with Horizon Bank?\n\nAnswer: - You are eligible to apply for a Horizon Bank Savings Account if you meet both of the following criteria:\n  {{faq_46c43248_001}}. You are a Singapore citizen, a Singapore permanent resident, or a foreign national holding a valid work pass.\n  {{faq_46c43248_002}}. You are {{faq_46c43248_003}} years of age or older.\n\n---\n\n[Task task_2 | Parent faq_7883a8c2]\nQuestion: My Horizon card is missing—what steps should I take?\n\nAnswer: - If you cannot locate your Horizon card, you can temporarily freeze it through the Horizon App:\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_001}}. Sign in to the Horizon App.\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_002}}. On the card overview screen, tap \"View & Manage Card.\"\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_003}}. Select \"Freeze Card.\"\n- For a card that is lost or stolen, first freeze it and then request a replacement:\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_004}}. Log into the Horizon App.\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_005}}. Open the card dashboard and choose \"View & Manage Card.\"\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_006}}. Tap \"Freeze Card\" followed by \"Order Replacement.\"\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_007}}. Horizon will issue a new card and permanently deactivate the old one.\n- You may also wish to file a police report.\n- The new card will arrive with a different card number; be sure to update any recurring payments (e.g., subscriptions) with the new details.\n- For additional assistance, select \"Contact Us\" from the app menu.\n\n---\n\n[Task task_3 | Parent faq_502da680]\nQuestion: What are the initial steps to begin buying and selling securities with Horizon Bank?\n\nAnswer: To initiate trading activities, it is necessary to establish a securities trading account. This can be accomplished by navigating to the Horizon App, selecting the Investments option, and then choosing the Stocks feature. Upon doing so, adhere to the on-screen prompts to finalize the account setup. Please be aware that the approval to open this account is contingent upon an internal evaluation conducted by Horizon Bank.\n\n---\n\n[Task task_3 | Parent faq_e94ad933]\nQuestion: What are the eligibility criteria for creating a Stocks account with Horizon Bank?\n\nAnswer: To be eligible for a Stocks account, you must meet the following conditions: \n      * You should have an active Savings account with Horizon Bank. If you haven't already, you can easily open one through the Horizon App.\n      * Your age should be between {{faq_e94ad933_001}} and {{faq_e94ad933_002}} years. Additionally, please be aware that individuals classified as US persons are not eligible to open a Stocks account with Horizon Bank.\"\n\n    Selected Approved Knowledge Used for This Response:\n    \"[Task task_1 | Opening a Savings Account | Parent faq_70aebcd6]\\nQuestion: What information and tools are necessary to open a Savings Account with Horizon Bank?\n\nAnswer: - A mobile phone together with MyInfo verification to auto‑populate your application form.\n- If you delete or reinstall the Horizon App after successfully registering, you will still need to authenticate via SingPass when you log in again.\\n\\n---\\n\\n[Task task_1 | Opening a Savings Account | Parent faq_46c43248]\\nQuestion: Can I open a Savings Account with Horizon Bank?\n\nAnswer: - You are eligible to apply for a Horizon Bank Savings Account if you meet both of the following criteria:\n  {{faq_46c43248_001}}. You are a Singapore citizen, a Singapore permanent resident, or a foreign national holding a valid work pass.\n  {{faq_46c43248_002}}. You are {{faq_46c43248_003}} years of age or older.\\n\\n---\\n\\n[Task task_2 | Replacing a Lost Card | Parent faq_7883a8c2]\\nQuestion: My Horizon card is missing—what steps should I take?\n\nAnswer: - If you cannot locate your Horizon card, you can temporarily freeze it through the Horizon App:\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_001}}. Sign in to the Horizon App.\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_002}}. On the card overview screen, tap \"View & Manage Card.\"\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_003}}. Select \"Freeze Card.\"\n- For a card that is lost or stolen, first freeze it and then request a replacement:\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_004}}. Log into the Hor