 the old one.\n- You may also wish to file a police report.\n- The new card will arrive with a different card number; be sure to update any recurring payments (e.g., subscriptions) with the new details.\n- For additional assistance, select \"Contact Us\" from the app menu.\n\n---\n\n[Task task_1 | Parent faq_33f045af]\nQuestion: My Horizon card has been compromised due to physical damage. What steps should I take to obtain a new one from Horizon Bank?\n\nAnswer: To acquire a replacement card, follow these straightforward steps: \n    * Access your Horizon App account \n    * Navigate to the 'Card Management' section \n    * Choose the 'Replace Current Card' option \n    * Indicate that your card is damaged to complete the request\n\n---\n\n[Task task_1 | Parent faq_98eb6af4]\nQuestion: I'm currently using my Horizon Link Credit/Debit Card, but my Horizon App displays the NTUC Link Credit/Debit Card. How can I obtain a physical version of the NTUC Link Credit/Debit Card?\n\nAnswer: To receive a physical NTUC Link Credit/Debit Card, you'll need to initiate a lost card replacement process through the Horizon App. It's essential to choose the correct replacement option, as selecting 'damaged card' will not yield the desired outcome. Please be aware that replacing your card will result in changes to your card details, including the card number, CVV, and expiry date. Consequently, you will need to update your card information for any existing online credit card arrangements, such as card-on-file and recurring payments, to ensure uninterrupted service.\n\n---\n\n[Task task_2 | Parent faq_7883a8c2]\nQuestion: My Horizon card is missing—what steps should I take?\n\nAnswer: - If you cannot locate your Horizon card, you can temporarily freeze it through the Horizon App:\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_001}}. Sign in to the Horizon App.\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_002}}. On the card overview screen, tap \"View & Manage Card.\"\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_003}}. Select \"Freeze Card.\"\n- For a card that is lost or stolen, first freeze it and then request a replacement:\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_004}}. Log into the Horizon App.\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_005}}. Open the card dashboard and choose \"View & Manage Card.\"\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_006}}. Tap \"Freeze Card\" followed by \"Order Replacement.\"\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_007}}. Horizon will issue a new card and permanently deactivate the old one.\n- You may also wish to file a police report.\n- The new card will arrive with a different card number; be sure to update any recurring payments (e.g., subscriptions) with the new details.\n- For additional assistance, select \"Contact Us\" from the app menu.\n\n---\n\n[Task task_2 | Parent faq_33f045af]\nQuestion: My Horizon card has been compromised due to physical damage. What steps should I take to obtain a new one from Horizon Bank?\n\nAnswer: To acquire a replacement card, follow these straightforward steps: \n    * Access your Horizon App account \n    * Navigate to the 'Card Management' section \n    * Choose the 'Replace Current Card' option \n    * Indicate that your card is damaged to complete the request\"\n\n    Selected Approved Knowledge Used for This Response:\n    \"[Task task_1 | Card Replacement for Credit and Debit Cards | Parent faq_7883a8c2]\\nQuestion: My Horizon card is missing—what steps should I take?\n\nAnswer: - If you cannot locate your Horizon card, you can temporarily freeze it through the Horizon App:\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_001}}. Sign in to the Horizon App.\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_002}}. On the card overview screen, tap \"View & Manage Card.\"\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_003}}. Select \"Freeze Card.\"\n- For a card that is lost or stolen, first freeze it and then request a replacement:\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_004}}. Log into the Horizon App.\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_005}}. Open the card dashboard and choose \"View & Manage Card.\"\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_006}}. Tap \"Freeze Card\" followed by \"Order Replacement.\"\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_007}}. Horizon will issue a new card and permanently deactivate the old one.\n- You may also wish to file a police report.\n- The new card will arrive with a different card number; be sure to update any recurring payments (e.g., subscriptions) with the new details.\n- For additional assistance, select \"Contact Us\" from the app menu.\\n\\n---\\n\\n[Task task_1 | Card Replacement for Credit and Debit Cards | Parent faq_33f045af]\\nQuestion: My Horizon card has been compromised due to physical damage. What steps should I take to obtain a new one from Horizon Bank?\n\nAnswer: To acquire a replacement card, follow these straightforward steps: \n    * Access your Horizon App account \n    * Navigate to the 'Card Management' section \n    * Choose the 'Replace Current Card' option \n    * Indicate that your card is damaged to complete the request\\n\\n---\\n\\n[Task task_1 | Card Replacement for Credit and Debit Cards | Parent faq_98eb6af4]\\nQuestion: I'm currently using my Horizon Link Credit/Debit Card, but my Horizon App displays the NTUC Link Credit/Debit Card. How can I obtain a physical version of the NTUC Link Credit/Debit Card?\n\nAnswer: To receive a physical NTUC Link Credit/Debit Card, you'll need to initiate a lost card replacement process through the Horizon App. It's essential to choose the correct replacement option, as selecting 'damaged card' will not yield the desired outcome. Please be aware that replacing your card will result in changes to your card details, including the card number, CVV, and expiry date. Consequently, you will need to update your card information for any existing online credit card arrangements, such as card-on-file and recurring payments, to ensure uninterrupted service.\\n\\n---\\n\\n[Task task_2 | Debit Card Replacement | Parent faq_7883a8c2]\\nQuestion: My Horizon card is missing—what steps should I take?\n\nAnswer: - If you cannot locate your Horizon card, you can temporarily freeze it through the Horizon App:\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_001}}. Sign in to the Horizon App.\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_002}}. On the card overview screen, tap \"View & Manage Card.\"\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_003}}. Select \"Freeze Card.\"\n- For a card that is lost or stolen, first freeze it and then request a replacement:\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_004}}. Log into the Horizon App.\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_005}}. Open the card dashboard and choose \"View & Manage Card.\"\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_006}}. Tap \"Freeze Card\" followed by \"Order Replacement.\"\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_007}}. Horizon will issue a new card and permanently deactivate the old one.\n- You may also wish to file a police report.\n- The new card will arrive with a different card number; be sure to update any recurring payments (e.g., subscriptions) with the new details.\n- For additional assistance, select \"Contact Us\" from the app menu.\\n\\n---\\n\\n[Task task_2 | Debit Card Replacement | Parent faq_33f045af]\\nQuestion: My Horizon card has been compromised due to physical damage. What steps should I take to obtain a new one from Horizon Bank?\n\nAnswer: To acquire a replacement card, follow these straightforward steps: \n    * Access your Horizon App account \n    * Navigate to the 'Card Management' section \n    * Choose the 'Replace Current Card' option \n    * Indicate that your card is damaged to complete the request\"\n\n    Unapproved Retrieved Knowledge for Clarification Suggestions:\n    \"\"\n\n    Intent Clarification Tasks Derived From the User Request:\n    \"[]\"\n\n    Durable Memory Context for Initial Greeting Only:\n    \"Latest Session Memory:\nCredit card eligibility: Singapore citizens/PRs 21‑55 need ≥S$30k annual income; >55 need ≥S$15k. Foreign nationals with work pass 21‑55 need ≥S$60k; >55 also ≥S$60k. Applications require Singapore residency, SingPass/MyInfo via Horizon app; processing up to 5 business days. To open an account, launch Horizon app and log in with SingPass. For a lost card, use the app’s card dashboard to freeze the card and order a replacement.\n\nUser Baseline Memory:\nCustomer is interested in Horizon Bank credit cards. E