}}. Select \"Freeze Card.\"\n- For a card that is lost or stolen, first freeze it and then request a replacement:\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_004}}. Log into the Horizon App.\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_005}}. Open the card dashboard and choose \"View & Manage Card.\"\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_006}}. Tap \"Freeze Card\" followed by \"Order Replacement.\"\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_007}}. Horizon will issue a new card and permanently deactivate the old one.\n- You may also wish to file a police report.\n- The new card will arrive with a different card number; be sure to update any recurring payments (e.g., subscriptions) with the new details.\n- For additional assistance, select \"Contact Us\" from the app menu.\\n\\n---\\n\\n[Task task_3 | Stocks Account Eligibility | Parent faq_e94ad933]\\nQuestion: What are the eligibility criteria for creating a Stocks account with Horizon Bank?\n\nAnswer: To be eligible for a Stocks account, you must meet the following conditions: \n      * You should have an active Savings account with Horizon Bank. If you haven't already, you can easily open one through the Horizon App.\n      * Your age should be between {{faq_e94ad933_001}} and {{faq_e94ad933_002}} years. Additionally, please be aware that individuals classified as US persons are not eligible to open a Stocks account with Horizon Bank.\"\n\n    Unapproved Retrieved Knowledge Permitted Only for Terminal Retrieval Clarification:\n    \"\"\n\n    Intent-clarification and greeting sources:\n    \"{\"intent_tasks\": [], \"greeting_memory\": \"Latest Session Memory:\\nDiscussed opening a Horizon Savings account: requires Singapore residency (citizen, PR, or work pass), MyInfo‑linked mobile, application via Horizon app in Singapore, submission minutes, up to five business days. Card loss: freeze card in app then order replacement; same process for credit and debit cards, choose “Lost card”. Stocks account: need active Savings account, age 18‑74, non‑US persons, set up in app under Investments→Stocks, internal approval, fund from Savings to trade.\\n\\nUser Baseline Memory:\\nCustomer can open a Horizon Savings account if they are a Singapore citizen, permanent resident, or hold a valid work pass, are at least 16 years old, have a MyInfo‑linked mobile number and SingPass login; application via the Horizon app takes minutes to submit and up to five business days to process. For lost credit or debit cards, they should freeze the card in the app and order a replacement via the “Lost card” option. Credit‑card eligibility: Singapore citizens/PRs 21‑55 need annual income ≥S$30,000 (≥S$15,000 if over 55); foreign nationals with a work pass need ≥S$60,000 regardless of age. To trade stocks, the customer needs an active Savings account, must be 18‑74 years old, not a US person, and set up the securities account in the app under Investments→Stocks after internal approval and funding from the Savings account.\"}\"\n\n    Customer-Facing Answer:\n    \"Confirm you are a Singapore resident (citizen, PR, or work pass holder); accounts cannot be opened from abroad.\n\nPrepare MyInfo verification using your mobile phone – the app will auto‑populate your details.\n\nSubmit the application through the Horizon app; the submission takes a few minutes and may take up to five business days to complete.\n\nAll actions are performed within the app, and you will receive notifications about your application status.\n\nSign in to Horizon App\n\nView and manage card\n\nFreeze and replace card\n\n\n\nTo be eligible for a Horizon Stocks account, you must meet the following criteria:\nHold an active Horizon Savings account (open one via the Horizon app if you don’t have it).\nBe between {{faq_e94ad933_001}} and {{faq_e94ad933_002}} years old.\nNot be classified as a US person.\"\n\n    Customer-Facing Clarification:\n    \"\"\n\n    Complete Customer-Facing UI Payload:\n    \"{\"uiType\": \"blocks\", \"options\": [], \"stepDetails\": [], \"listTitle\": \"\", \"listIntro\": \"\", \"items\": [], \"extendedText\"