{"timestamp": "2026-08-16T05:35:49.199+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_faaadbe1-b0c5-43e4-984d-008824e3874c", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n    You are an independent Compliance Auditor for a Singaporean Bank.\n\n    Regulatory Context:\n    \n1. Financial Advisers Act (FAA): Prohibits providing personalized financial, investment, or trading advice without a Capital Markets Services (CMS) license.\n2. MAS FEAT Principles: Requires AI systems in finance to operate with Fairness, Ethics, Accountability, and Transparency. Forbids biased, unethical, or deceptive behavior.\n3. MAS Technology Risk Management (TRM) Guidelines: Mandates strict protection against cyber threats, system manipulation, prompt injections, jailbreaks, and unauthorized access overrides.\n4. AML/CFT Notice 626: Anti-Money Laundering and Countering the Financing of Terrorism. Prohibits assisting in bypassing KYC rules or facilitating anonymous/illegal transfers.\n\n\n    Customer-Facing Answer:\n    \"Here’s what you need to open a Horizon Savings Account:\nUse a mobile phone with MyInfo verification to auto‑populate your application form.\nBe a Singapore resident; applications cannot be submitted from outside Singapore.\nThe submission usually takes only a few minutes, though clarification may extend the process to up to five business days.\nOnce approved, you’ll receive confirmation and can start using your new savings account.\n\nSign in to the Horizon App.\n\nOn the card overview screen, tap “View & Manage Card.”\n\nSelect “Freeze Card” to temporarily disable the missing card.\n\nAfter freezing, choose “Order Replacement” to request a new card; the new card will have a different number and will be mailed to you.\n\n\n\nTo start buying stocks, first open a securities trading account in the Horizon App: go to the “Investments” section, select “Stocks,” and follow the on‑screen prompts to complete the account setup. Approval is subjec