{"timestamp": "2026-08-16T07:24:11.831+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_ec07a93d-8eb9-4aeb-911d-0b03b99c1416", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n    You are an evidence-groundedness auditor for a read-only Horizon Bank FAQ assistant.\n\n    User Request: \"How do I open an account, I lost my credit card, and how can I start buying stocks?\"\n    Is Initial Greeting: False\n\n    Selected Approved Knowledge for the Answer:\n    \"[Task task_1 | Opening a Savings Account | Parent faq_70aebcd6]\\nQuestion: What information and tools are necessary to open a Savings Account with Horizon Bank?\n\nAnswer: - A mobile phone together with MyInfo verification to auto‑populate your application form.\n- If you delete or reinstall the Horizon App after successfully registering, you will still need to authenticate via SingPass when you log in again.\\n\\n---\\n\\n[Task task_2 | Lost Credit Card Procedure | Parent faq_7883a8c2]\\nQuestion: My Horizon card is missing—what steps should I take?\n\nAnswer: - If you cannot locate your Horizon card, you can temporarily freeze it through the Horizon App:\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_001}}. Sign in to the Horizon App.\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_002}}. On the card overview screen, tap \"View & Manage Card.\"\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_003}}. Select \"Freeze Card.\"\n- For a card that is lost or stolen, first freeze it and then request a replacement:\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_004}}. Log into the Horizon App.\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_005}}. Open the card dashboard and choose \"View & Manage Card.\"\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_006}}. Tap \"Freeze Card\" followed by \"Order Replacement.\"\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_007}}. Horizon will issue a new card and permanently deactivate the old one.\n- You may also wish to file a police report.\n- The new card will arrive with a different card number; be sure to update any recurring payments (e.g., subscriptions) with the new details.\n- For additional assistance, select \"Contact Us\" from the app menu.\\n\\n---\\n\\n[Task task_3 | Stocks Account Requirements | Parent faq_502da680]\\nQuestion: What are the initial steps to begin buying and selling securities with Horizon Bank?\n\nAnswer: To initiate trading activities, it is necessary to establish a securities trading account. This can be accomplished by navigating to the Horizon App, selecting the Investments option, and then choosing the Stocks feature. Upon doing so, adhere to the on-screen prompts to finalize the account setup. Please be aware that the approval to open this account is contingent upon an internal evaluation conducted by Horizon Bank.\\n\\n---\\n\\n[Task task_3 | Stocks Account Requirements | Parent faq_e94ad933]\\nQuestion: What are the eligibility criteria for creating a Stocks account with Horizon Bank?\n\nAnswer: To be eligible for a Stocks account, you must meet the following conditions: \n      * You should have an active Savings account with Horizon Bank. If you haven't already, you can easily open one through the Horizon App.\n      * Your age should be between {{faq_e94ad933_001}} and {{faq_e94ad933_002}} years. Additionally, please be aware that individuals classified as US persons are not eligible to open a Stocks account with Horizon Bank.\"\n\n    Unapproved Retrieved Knowledge Permitted Only for Terminal Retrieval Clarification:\n    \"\"\n\n    Intent-clarification and greeting sources:\n    \"{\"intent_tasks\": [], \"greeting_memory\": \"Latest Session Memory:\\nTo replace a lost credit card, sign in to the Horizon App, navigate to the card overview screen, select 'View & Manage Card,' choose 'Freeze Card,' and select 'Order Replacement.' The new card will have a different number, requiring updates to recurring payments.\\n\\nUser Baseline Memory:\\nCustomer is a Singapore resident eligible for Horizon banking products. Credit card eligibility requires minimum annual income: S$30k for citizens/PRs aged 21-55, S$15k for those >55; S$60k for foreign nationals with work passes. Savings account opening requires MyInfo-linked mobile and SingPass. Securities trading requires an active Savings account, age 18-74, and non-US person status. Lost credit or debit cards are managed via the Horizon app by freezing the card and ordering a replacement, which results in a new card number.\"}\"\n\n    Customer-Facing Answer:\n    \"To open a Savings Account with Horizon Bank, you will need your mobile phone and MyInfo verification to auto-populate your application form. Please note that if you delete or reinstall the Horizon App after registering, you will need to authenticate via SingPass when logging in again.\n\nSign in to the Horizon App.\n\nOn the card overview screen, tap \"View & Manage Card.\"\n\nSelect \"Freeze Card.\"\n\nChoose \"Order Replacement\" to have a new card issued and the old one permanently deactivated.\n\nOnce you have frozen your card, you can request a replacement through the card dashboard. Please be aware that your new card will arrive with a different card number, so you will need to update any recurring payments or subscriptions. You may also wish to file a police report for a lost or stolen card.\n\nTo begin buying and selling stocks, you must first establish a securities trading account through the Horizon App by selecting 'Investments' and then 'Stocks'.\nYou must have an active Savings account with Horizon Bank.\nYou must be between 18 and 74 years of age.\nYou must not be classified as a US person.\nAccount approval is subject to an internal evaluation by Horizon Bank.\nFollow the on-screen prompts in the Stocks feature to finalize your setup.\"\n\n    Customer-Facing Clarification:\n    \"\"\n\n    Complete Customer-Facing UI Payload:\n    \"{\"uiType\": \"blocks\", \"options\": [], \"stepDetails\": [], \"listTitle\": \"\", \"listIntro\": \"\", \"items\": [], \"extendedText\": \"\", \"listClarificationText\": \"\", \"responseBlocks\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"To open a Savings Account with Horizon Bank, you will ne