ieval Clarification:\n    \"[Task task_1 | Unapproved Parent faq_c8d61dc6]\nQuestion: What investment opportunities are available through Horizon Bank's stock trading services?\n\nAnswer: Horizon Bank provides its clients with the ability to engage in trading activities involving stocks and exchange-traded funds listed on US exchanges, in addition to a selection of UK UCITS exchange-traded funds.\n\n---\n\n[Task task_1 | Unapproved Parent faq_8d322d06]\nQuestion: What range of financial products and services does Horizon Bank provide to its customers?\n\nAnswer: Horizon Bank is pleased to introduce an initial suite of products, including a Horizon credit card, a savings account, and personal accident insurance for families. These offerings are complemented by a best-in-class rewards and loyalty program, seamlessly integrated with the FairPrice Group ecosystem. Furthermore, Horizon Bank has collaborated with prominent brands such as KFC, Starbucks, Viu, and Caltex to bring exclusive deals, providing our customers with additional savings opportunities. This marks the beginning of our product development journey, and we look forward to working closely with our customers to further enhance and expand our offerings.\n\n---\n\n[Task task_1 | Unapproved Parent faq_2f201863]\nQuestion: What steps are required to activate the automatic investment feature for equities at Horizon Bank?\n\nAnswer: To initiate automatic investments in stocks with Horizon Bank, ensure you have an active stocks account. Follow these steps: \n   * Access the Horizon App and navigate to the Investments section\n   * Select the Stocks option\n   * Proceed to the setup for automatic investments\n   * Identify the specific stock or exchange-traded fund you wish to invest in automatically\n   * Determine your preferred investment schedule and commencement date; if not specified, the next working day will be applied by default\n   * Specify the amount and currency for regular investments\n   * Review the details and confirm the setup to complete the process\n\n---\n\n[Task task_1 | Unapproved Parent faq_4bd34aa4]\nQuestion: At Horizon Bank, what is the lowest investment threshold for purchasing securities?\n\nAnswer: With Horizon Bank, you have the flexibility to initiate your investment portfolio by buying stocks and ETFs with a minimum investment of just USD {{faq_4bd34aa4_001}}.\n\n---\n\n[Task task_2 | Unapproved Parent faq_10f9fec0]\nQuestion: What are the requirements to open a new Horizon Bank account?\n\nAnswer: To initiate the application process for a Horizon Bank account, simply utilize your mobile device and authenticate through MyInfo, which will expedite the pre-filling of your application in a secure manner. For non-Singaporean residents, please be prepared to upload a valid passport and relevant income documentation, particularly if you are applying for a Horizon credit card.\n\n---\n\n[Task task_2 | Unapproved Parent faq_ded247c0]\nQuestion: What sets Horizon Bank apart from traditional banking institutions?\n\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, we've revolutionized the banking experience by leveraging cutting-edge technology to create a seamless, mobile-first platform. By streamlining processes and eliminating the need for physical branches, we're able to provide our customers with a {{faq_ded247c0_001}}/{{faq_ded247c0_002}} banking service that's both convenient and efficient. A prime illustration of this is our expedited sign-up process, which can be completed in mere minutes for Singapore residents utilizing Singpass, highlighting our commitment to simplicity and speed.\n\n---\n\n[Task task_2 | Unapproved Parent faq_2fe9ef88]\nQuestion: I'm experiencing difficulties with the Horizon Bank mobile application. How can I obtain technical assistance?\n\nAnswer: To resolve the issue, you can reach out to our dedicated support team through the in-app messaging feature or by dialing +{{faq_2fe9ef88_001}} {{faq_2fe9ef88_002}}-HORIZON (+{{faq_2fe9ef88_003}} {{faq_2fe9ef88_004}} {{faq_2fe9ef88_005}}) for personalized guidance.\n\n---\n\n[Task task_2 | Unapproved Parent faq_b6934e37]\nQuestion: Are investments with Horizon Bank limited to cash transactions, or can I utilize my CPF or SRS account?\n\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, our investment platform currently only accommodates cash transactions for trading stocks and ETFs. Unfortunately, this means that funds from CPF or SRS accounts are not eligible for use in these investment activities at this time.\"\n\n    Intent-clarification and greeting sources:\n    \"{\"intent_tasks\": [], \"greeting_memory\": \"Latest Session Memory:\\nHorizon Bank securities trading requires an active Savings account, age 18-74, and non-US person status. Users must open a Stocks account via the Investments section in the Horizon App, subject to internal approval. Automated recurring investments are funded by deducting SGD from the Savings account, converted to USD at current rates. Sufficient funds must be available in the Savings account prior to the scheduled transaction date.\\n\\nUser Baseline Memory:\\nCustomer holds a Horizon Savings account. Securities trading eligibility requires age 18-74, non-US person status, and internal approval. Recurring investments are funded via SGD deduction from the Savings account, converted to USD. Lost credit card replacement is managed via the Horizon App, resulting in a new card number that requires manual updates to recurring payments.\"}\"\n\n    Customer-Facing Answer:\n    \"To set up recurring automatic investments in individual stocks, you must first ensure you have an active Stocks account. You can initiate this by navigating to the Investments section in the Horizon App, selecting the Stocks option, and following the prompts to configure your automatic investment schedule, including the specific stock, investment amount, and frequency. Regarding eligibility, please note that securities trading is available to customers aged 18-74 who are non-US persons