fficient funds for your automated investments. However, I do not have access to the specific eligibility requirements for securities trading or the procedural steps for setting up the feature in the app. Would you like me to clarify these specific points?\"\n\n    Complete Customer-Facing UI Payload:\n    \"{\"uiType\": \"blocks\", \"options\": [], \"stepDetails\": [], \"listTitle\": \"\", \"listIntro\": \"\", \"items\": [], \"extendedText\": \"\", \"listClarificationText\": \"\", \"responseBlocks\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"For your automated investments, Horizon Bank automatically deducts the required amount from your Horizon Savings account in Singapore Dollars, which is then converted to US Dollars at the current exchange rate. You do not need to preload your investment account, and you will receive a notification one day before the scheduled investment. Please ensure your Savings account has sufficient funds to cover the transaction, as the investment will be skipped if the balance is low. If a transaction is skipped, you will be notified, and the system will automatically attempt the next scheduled investment provided your configuration remains active.\\n\\nWhile the system will not retry a skipped transaction on the original date, you may manually place an order through the Horizon App after replenishing your account.\", \"items\": [], \"options\": [], \"progressTitle\": \"\", \"stepDetails\": [], \"currentStep\": null, \"totalSteps\": null, \"listTitle\": \"\", \"listIntro\": \"\", \"extendedText\": \"\"}, {\"type\": \"clarification\", \"text\": \"I have provided the details regarding the funding process and how Horizon Bank handles insufficient funds for your automated investments. However, I do not have access to the specific eligibility requirements for securities trading or the procedural steps for setting up the feature in the app. Would you like me to clarify these specific points?\"}]}\"\n\n    TASK: Assess COMPLIANCE ONLY. Do not assess whether facts are supported by\n    evidence; a separate auditor handles groundedness. Determine whether any\n    customer-facing text, UI item, option, step, list entry, or extended text\n    provides unauthorized personalized financial advice, subjective product\n    recommendation, return forecast, transaction execution, deceptive claim,\n    or assistance to bypass security, KYC, AML/CFT, or other controls.\n    Neutral factual information, safe apologies, and neutral clarification\n    requests are compliant. Every visible field in the payload is in scope.\n\n    Output JSON only:\n    {\"passed\": true/false, \"reason\": \"...\", \"rewrite_instruction\": \"...\"}\n    "}
