 requirements but do not specify the eligibility requirements for opening an investment account specifically for trading individual stocks.\", \"unapproved_parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_10f9fec0\", \"content\": \"Question: What are the requirements to open a new Horizon Bank account?\\n\\nAnswer: To initiate the application process for a Horizon Bank account, simply utilize your mobile device and authenticate through MyInfo, which will expedite the pre-filling of your application in a secure manner. For non-Singaporean residents, please be prepared to upload a valid passport and relevant income documentation, particularly if you are applying for a Horizon credit card.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_41bb5359\", \"content\": \"Question: How do investment accounts at Horizon Bank differ from traditional savings accounts in terms of their usage and benefits?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, our investment accounts are specifically designed for trading stocks and ETFs, and they do not offer the same flexibility as our savings accounts for everyday banking needs. Notably, these investment accounts do not accrue interest and are not protected under the Deposit Insurance Scheme, which is managed by the Singapore Deposit Insurance Corporation (SDIC), unlike our savings accounts.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_b6934e37\", \"content\": \"Question: Are investments with Horizon Bank limited to cash transactions, or can I utilize my CPF or SRS account?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, our investment platform currently only accommodates cash transactions for trading stocks and ETFs. Unfortunately, this means that funds from CPF or SRS accounts are not eligible for use in these investment activities at this time.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_d18f8450\", \"content\": \"Question: As an existing customer of another bank, am I eligible for a Horizon Bank account by default?\\n\\nAnswer: Having an account with another institution does not automatically qualify you for a Horizon Bank account. However, you can easily register for a Horizon Bank account through the Horizon App in a matter of minutes, allowing you to start benefiting from discounts on your daily expenses right away.\"}]}, {\"task_id\": \"task_3\", \"type\": \"TERMINAL_RETRIEVAL_FEEDBACK\", \"feedback\": \"How do I set up recurring automatic investments for stocks and what are the funding mechanisms for these purchases?\", \"reason\": \"The provided parents do not explain how to set up recurring automatic investments or how those specific purchases are funded, other than noting that CPF/SRS funds are not eligible.\", \"unapproved_parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_b73dbebe\", \"content\": \"Question: Does Horizon Bank offer personalized investment guidance to its clients?\\n\\nAnswer: Horizon Bank maintains a neutral stance and does not extend investment advice to its customers, allowing them to make independent decisions regarding their financial portfolios.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_b8e22edc\", \"content\": \"Question: How does Horizon Bank's fee structure work for investment transactions?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, we provide a competitive fee environment for our investors. Until December {{faq_b8e22edc_001}}, {{faq_b8e22edc_002}}, trading US stocks and ETFs is commission-free. After this period, a commission of {{faq_b8e22edc_003}} applies, with a minimum charge of USD {{faq_b8e22edc_004}} per trade. For UK UCITS ETFs, a commission rate of {{faq_b8e22edc_005}} is applicable, with a minimum fee of USD {{faq_b8e22edc_006}} per trade. Additionally, a {{faq_b8e22edc_007}} GST is levied on commissions, and your Trade Confirmation will also serve as your Tax Invoice. Notably, Horizon Bank does not impose platform, custody, settlement, or corporate action handling fees. For a detailed breakdown, please navigate to the Horizon App, select your Profile, and then access the Legal section to view the Stocks Fee Schedule.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_2fe8118e\", \"content\": \"Question: What steps must I follow to have government payouts deposited into my Horizon savings account?\\n\\nAnswer: - To receive the funds, enrol your NRIC with PayNow via the Horizon app.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_41bb5359\", \"content\": \"Question: How do investment accounts at Horizon Bank differ from traditional savings accounts in terms of their usage and benefits?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, our investment accounts are specifically designed for trading stocks and ETFs, and they do not offer the same flexibility as our savings accounts for everyday banking needs. Notably, these investment accounts do not accrue interest and are not protected under the Deposit Insurance Scheme, which is managed by the Singapore Deposit Insurance Corporation (SDIC), unlike our savings accounts.\"}]}]\n    Failed outbound-audit feedback from the prior generation attempt:\n    [\"Groundedness audit failed: Incorporate the eligibility requirements (age 18-74, non-US person status) and funding details (SGD deduction from the Savings account, converted to USD) from the User Baseline Memory into the response, as these are grounded facts available to the assistant.\"]\n\n    Rules:\n    - Use Current Session Trusted History as the primary continuity context for\n      references to an earlier answer, correction, comparison, or follow-up.\n      Use Current-Session Rolling Context only to extend older same-session\n      context. Last Session Recall and User Baseline Memory are lower-priority\n      advisory context: never revive an old topic, request, issue, or workflow\n      unless the latest customer request explicitly refers to it.\n    - Conversation context is NOT banking evidence. It may help you understand\n      what the customer means, but every factual claim, instruction,\n      comparison, UI item, extended_text item, and option must be supported by\n      the current block's approved parents. If current evidence differs from a\n      prior assistant response, follow the current approved evidence.\n  