 item, option, step, list entry, or extended text\n    provides unauthorized personalized financial advice, subjective product\n    recommendation, return forecast, transaction execution, deceptive claim,\n    or assistance to bypass security, KYC, AML/CFT, or other controls.\n    Neutral factual information, safe apologies, and neutral clarification\n    requests are compliant. Every visible field in the payload is in scope.\n\n    Output JSON only:\n    {\"passed\": true/false, \"reason\": \"...\", \"rewrite_instruction\": \"...\"}\n    "}
{"timestamp": "2026-08-16T10:57:46.267+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_74c3c0f2-4d6d-454a-a770-66d1addeded7", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n    You are an evidence-groundedness auditor for a read-only Horizon Bank FAQ assistant.\n\n    User Request: \"How do I set up recurring automatic investments in individual stocks, what are the eligibility requirements, and how will the purchases be funded?\"\n    Is Initial Greeting: False\n\n    Selected Approved Knowledge for the Answer:\n    \"[Task task_1 | Parent faq_9a88fadb]\\nQuestion: Is it possible to configure multiple automated investment plans for equities through Horizon Bank?\n\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, you have the flexibility to establish numerous automated investment schedules for your stock portfolio, including multiple plans for the same security with varying frequencies. Furthermore, you can modify or terminate these instructions at any time, with changes taking effect from the next scheduled investment date.\\n\\n---\\n\\n[Task task_1 | Parent faq_2f201863]\\nQuestion: What steps are required to activate the automatic investment feature for equities at Horizon Bank?\n\nAnswer: To initiate automatic investments in stocks with Horizon Bank, ensure you have an active stocks account. Follow these steps: \n   * Access the Horizon App and navigate to the Investments section\n   * Select the Stocks option\n   * Proceed to the setup for automatic investments\n   * Identify the specific stock or exchange-traded fund you wish to invest in automatically\n   * Determine your preferred investment schedule and commencement date; if not specified, the next working day will be applied by default\n   * Specify the amount and currency for regular investments\n   * Review the details and confirm the setup to complete the process\"\n\n    Unapproved Retrieved Knowledge Permitted Only for Terminal Retrieval Clarification:\n    \"[Task task_2 | Unapproved Parent faq_10f9fec0]\nQuestion: What are the requirements to open a new Horizon Bank account?\n\nAnswer: To initiate the application process for a Horizon Bank account, simply utilize your mobile device and authenticate through MyInfo, which will expedite the pre-filling of your application in a secure manner. For non-Singaporean residents, please be prepared to upload a valid passport and relevant income documentation, particularly if you are applying for a Horizon credit card.\n\n---\n\n[Task task_2 | Unapproved Parent faq_41bb5359]\nQuestion: How do investment accounts at Horizon Bank differ from traditional savings accounts in terms of their usage and benefits?\n\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, our investment accounts are specifically designed for trading stocks and ETFs, and they do not offer the same flexibility as our savings accounts for everyday banking needs. Notably, these investment accounts do not accrue interest and are not protected under the Deposit Insurance Scheme, which is managed by the Singapore Deposit Insurance Corporation (SDIC), unlike our savings accounts.\n\n---\n\n[Task task_2 | Unapproved Parent faq_b6934e37]\nQuestion: Are investments with Horizon Bank limited to cash transactions, or can I utilize my CPF or SRS account?\n\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, our investment platform currently only accommodates cash transactions for trading stocks and ETFs. Unfortunately, this means that funds from CPF or SRS accounts are not eligible for use in these investment activities at this time.\n\n---\n\n[Task task_2 | Unapproved Parent faq_d18f8450]\nQuestion: As an existing customer of another bank, am I eligible for a Horizon Bank account by default?\n\nAnswer: Having an account with another institution does not automatically qualify you for a Horizon Bank account. However, you can easily register for a Horizon Bank account through the Horizon App in a matter of minutes, allowing you to start benefiting from discounts on your daily expenses right away.\n\n---\n\n[Task task_3 | Unapproved Parent faq_b73dbebe]\nQuestion: Does Horizon Bank offer personalized investment guidance to its clients?\n\nAnswer: Horizon Bank maintains a neutral stance and does not extend investment advice to its customers, allowing them to make independent decisions regarding their financial portfolios.\n\n---\n\n[Task task_3 | Unapproved Parent faq_b8e22edc]\nQuestion: How does Horizon Bank's fee structure work for investment transactions?\n\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, we provide a competitive fee environment for our investors. Until December {{faq_b8e22edc_001}}, {{faq_b8e22edc_002}}, trading US stocks and ETFs is commission-free. After this period, a commission of {{faq_b8e22edc_003}} applies, with a minimum charge of USD {{faq_b8e22edc_004}} per trade. For UK UCITS ETFs, a commission rate of {{faq_b8e22edc_005}} is applicable, with a minimum fee of USD {{faq_b8e22edc_006}} per trade. Additionally, a {{faq_b8e22edc_007}} GST is levied on commissions, and your Trade Confirmation will also serve as your Tax Invoice. Notably, Horizon Bank does not impose platform, custody, settlement, or corporate action handling fees. For a detailed breakdown, please navigate to the Horizon App, select your Profile, and then access the Legal section to view the Stocks Fee Schedule.\n\n---\n\n[Task task_3 | Unapproved Parent faq_2fe8118e]\nQuestion: What steps must I follow to have government payouts deposited into my Horizon savings account?\n\nAnswer: - To receive the funds, enrol your NRIC with PayNow via the Horizon app.\n\n---\n\n[Task task_3 | Unapproved Parent faq_41bb5359]\nQuestion: How do investment accounts at Horizon Bank differ from traditional savings accounts in terms of their usage and benefits?\n\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, our investment accounts are specifically designed for trading stocks and ETFs, and they do not offer the same flexibility as our savings accounts for everyday banking needs. Notably, these investment accounts do not accrue interest and are not protected under the Deposit Insurance Scheme, which is managed by the Singapore Deposit Insurance Corporation (SDIC), unlike our savings accounts.\"\n\n    Intent-clarification and greeting sources:\n    \"{\"intent_tasks\": [], \"greeting_memory\": \"Latest Session Memory:\\nTo open a savings account, applicants must be Singapore residents applying locally. The process requires a mobile device for MyInfo verification. Reinstalling the Horizon App after registration necessitates SingPass authentication for subsequent logins.\\n\\nUser Baseline Memory:\\nCustomer is a Singapore resident. Banking requirements include a mobile device for MyInfo verification and SingPass for Horizon App authentication. Securities trading and recurring investments require an active Horizon Savings account, age 18-74, and non-US person status. Recurring investments are funded via SGD deduction from the Savings account, converted to USD at current rates, with notifications sent one day prior to scheduled purchases.\"}\"\n\n    Customer-Facing Answer:\n    \"Could you please clarify your request?\"\n\n    Customer-Facing Clarification:\n    \"Could you clarify what information you are looking for?\"\n\n    Complete Customer-Facing UI Payload:\n    \"{\"uiType\": \"blocks\", \"options\": [], \"stepDetails\": [], \"listTitle\": \"\", \"listIntro\": \"\", \"items\": [], \"extendedText\": \"\", \"listClarificationText\": \"\", \"responseBlocks\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Could you please clarify your request?\", \"items\": [], \"options\": [], \"progressTitle\": \"\", \"stepDetails\": [], \"currentStep\": null, \"totalSteps\": null, \"listTitle\": \"\", \"listIntro\": \"\", \"extendedText\": \"\"}, {\"type\": \"clarification\", \"text\": \"Could you clarify what information you are looking for?\"}]}\"\n\n    TASK: Assess GROUNDEDNESS ONLY. Do not assess MAS compliance, safety,\n    advice, or whether the answer is helpful.\n\n    - For a normal answer, every factual claim, instr