8450\", \"content\": \"Question: As an existing customer of another bank, am I eligible for a Horizon Bank account by default?\\n\\nAnswer: Having an account with another institution does not automatically qualify you for a Horizon Bank account. However, you can easily register for a Horizon Bank account through the Horizon App in a matter of minutes, allowing you to start benefiting from discounts on your daily expenses right away.\"}]}, {\"task_id\": \"task_3\", \"resolved_subquery\": \"how will the purchases be funded\", \"unapproved_parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_b73dbebe\", \"content\": \"Question: Does Horizon Bank offer personalized investment guidance to its clients?\\n\\nAnswer: Horizon Bank maintains a neutral stance and does not extend investment advice to its customers, allowing them to make independent decisions regarding their financial portfolios.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_b8e22edc\", \"content\": \"Question: How does Horizon Bank's fee structure work for investment transactions?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, we provide a competitive fee environment for our investors. Until December {{faq_b8e22edc_001}}, {{faq_b8e22edc_002}}, trading US stocks and ETFs is commission-free. After this period, a commission of {{faq_b8e22edc_003}} applies, with a minimum charge of USD {{faq_b8e22edc_004}} per trade. For UK UCITS ETFs, a commission rate of {{faq_b8e22edc_005}} is applicable, with a minimum fee of USD {{faq_b8e22edc_006}} per trade. Additionally, a {{faq_b8e22edc_007}} GST is levied on commissions, and your Trade Confirmation will also serve as your Tax Invoice. Notably, Horizon Bank does not impose platform, custody, settlement, or corporate action handling fees. For a detailed breakdown, please navigate to the Horizon App, select your Profile, and then access the Legal section to view the Stocks Fee Schedule.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_2fe8118e\", \"content\": \"Question: What steps must I follow to have government payouts deposited into my Horizon savings account?\\n\\nAnswer: - To receive the funds, enrol your NRIC with PayNow via the Horizon app.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_41bb5359\", \"content\": \"Question: How do investment accounts at Horizon Bank differ from traditional savings accounts in terms of their usage and benefits?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, our investment accounts are specifically designed for trading stocks and ETFs, and they do not offer the same flexibility as our savings accounts for everyday banking needs. Notably, these investment accounts do not accrue interest and are not protected under the Deposit Insurance Scheme, which is managed by the Singapore Deposit Insurance Corporation (SDIC), unlike our savings accounts.\"}]}]\n\n        Customer-Facing Answer:\n        \"Open the Horizon App and navigate to the Investments section, then select the Stocks option.\n\nProceed to the automatic investment setup, choose your desired stock or ETF, and define your investment schedule, commencement date, amount, and currency.\n\nReview your investment details carefully and confirm the setup to activate your recurring plan.\n\nAt Horizon Bank, you have the flexibility to manage your automated investments directly through the app. Please note that you must have an active stocks account to initiate these recurring investments.\"\n\n        Customer-Facing Clarification:\n        \"I have provided the steps to set up recurring investments and details on managing your plans. However, I do not have specific information regarding the eligibility requirements for opening an investment account or the specific funding mechanisms for these purchases beyond the fact that they are processed through your stocks account.\"\n\n        Complete Customer-Facing UI Payload:\n        \"{\"uiType\": \"blocks\", \"options\": [], \"stepDetails\": [], \"listTitle\": \"\", \"listIntro\": \"\", \"items\": [], \"extendedText\": \"\", \"listClarificationText\": \"\", \"responseBlocks\": [{\"type\": \"stepper\", \"text\": \"\",