hoices does Horizon Bank provide for its deposit accounts?\\n\\nAnswer: - Horizon Bank now lets you select a savings plan that determines the interest applied to the balance in your savings account. The three available options are **Signature**, **Zen**, and **Flex**.\\n- You may switch your plan at any time before the month ends; the new selection takes effect on the {{faq_7b5e0f27_001}}st day of the following month.\\n- Each successful change triggers an in‑app push notification and an email alert.\\n- To see which plan is currently active, open the **Horizon App**, navigate to **Savings > Interest This Month**, where you can also monitor your progress toward any bonus interest tied to the chosen plan.\\n- If you do not make a change during a given month, the existing plan automatically rolls over into the next month.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_7d49c937\", \"content\": \"Question: What are the available ways to fund my Horizon Bank savings account?\\n\\nAnswer: - **Method {{faq_7d49c937_001}} – Bank transfer via FAST**\\n  {{faq_7d49c937_002}}. Log in to the online portal of your other bank.\\n  {{faq_7d49c937_003}}. Add your Horizon Bank savings account as a local beneficiary, providing the beneficiary name and your Horizon savings account number.\\n  {{faq_7d49c937_004}}. Initiate the FAST transfer; the money will be credited to your Horizon account shortly.\\n- **Method {{faq_7d49c937_005}} – PayNow**\\n  {{faq_7d49c937_006}}. If your mobile number or NRIC/FIN is already linked to PayNow with a different bank, first remove that linkage.\\n  {{faq_7d49c937_007}}. Open the Horizon App, tap the Payments tab, and select “Register for PayNow” if you haven’t done so already.\\n  {{faq_7d49c937_008}}. Complete the registration, then send a PayNow payment to the registered mobile number or NRIC/FIN; the funds will appear in your Horizon savings account.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_41bb5359\", \"content\": \"Question: How do investment accounts at Horizon Bank differ from 