{"timestamp": "2026-08-17T17:29:36.725+00:00", "event": "llm.response", "session_id": "sess_e5ffd6da-0007-4e69-8d1f-bb800fd708e2", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "raw_response": "{\"blocks\":[{\"task_id\":\"task_1\",\"answer\":\"To set up AutoInvest for equities, open the Horizon App, go to Investments → Stocks, select Automatic investments, choose the stock or ETF, set your preferred schedule and start date (if not specified the next working day is used), and specify the amount and currency. The required amount will be deducted from your Horizon Savings account in Singapore Dollars, converted to US Dollars at the current exchange rate, and you will receive a notification one day before the scheduled investment. You may create multiple automated plans, and you can modify or terminate any plan at any time; changes take effect from the next scheduled investment date. If your Savings balance is insufficient, the investment is skipped, you are notified, and the system will attempt the investment again on the next scheduled date.\"},{\"task_id\":\"task_2\",\"answer\":\"The lowest amount you can invest in a stock or ETF is USD {{faq_4bd34aa4_001}}.\"},{\"task_id\":\"task_3\",\"answer\":\"You can modify or cancel any automated investment plan at any time, and the changes will apply from the next scheduled investment date. Trading US stocks and ETFs is commission‑free until December {{faq_b8e22edc_001}} ({{faq_b8e22edc_002}}). After that date a commission of {{faq_b8e22edc_003}} applies with a minimum charge of USD {{faq_b8e22edc_004}} per trade. For UK UCITS ETFs the commission is {{faq_b8e22edc_005}} with a minimum of USD {{faq_b8e22edc_006}} per trade. A GST of {{faq_b8e22edc_007}} is added on commissions, and there are no platform, custody, settlement, or corporate‑action handling fees.\"}],\"clarification\":\"\"}", "elapsed_ms": 4251.7}
