{"timestamp": "2026-08-17T17:29:37.346+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_e5ffd6da-0007-4e69-8d1f-bb800fd708e2", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n        NORMAL RESPONSE GROUNDEDNESS AUDIT\n        You are an evidence-groundedness auditor for a read-only Horizon Bank FAQ assistant.\n\n        Task-Level Approved Evidence (the only factual source for answers and answer UI):\n        [{\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"resolved_subquery\": \"How do recurring automatic investments work for a Stocks account?\", \"approved_parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_2f201863\", \"content\": \"Question: What steps are required to activate the automatic investment feature for equities at Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: To initiate automatic investments in stocks with Horizon Bank, ensure you have an active stocks account. Follow these steps: \\n   * Access the Horizon App and navigate to the Investments section\\n   * Select the Stocks option\\n   * Proceed to the setup for automatic investments\\n   * Identify the specific stock or exchange-traded fund you wish to invest in automatically\\n   * Determine your preferred investment schedule and commencement date; if not specified, the next working day will be applied by default\\n   * Specify the amount and currency for regular investments\\n   * Review the details and confirm the setup to complete the process\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_9a88fadb\", \"content\": \"Question: Is it possible to configure multiple automated investment plans for equities through Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, you have the flexibility to establish numerous automated investment schedules for your stock portfolio, including multiple plans for the same security with varying frequencies. Furthermore, you can modify or terminate these instructions at any time, with changes taking effect from the next scheduled investment date.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_3fb1caf7\", \"content\": \"Question: Is it necessary to preload my investment account for automated stock purchases?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, your automated investments are seamlessly facilitated without requiring a separate preload of funds. For each scheduled investment, the necessary amount will be automatically deducted from your Horizon Savings account in Singapore Dollars and converted to US Dollars at the current exchange rate. As a courtesy, you will receive a notification one day prior to the scheduled investment. To avoid any issues, please ensure that your Savings account with Horizon Bank has adequate funds to cover the upcoming investment.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_d22a7a8c\", \"content\": \"Question: How does Horizon Bank handle AutoInvest transactions when my Savings account balance is low?\\n\\nAnswer: In the event that your Savings account lacks sufficient funds to cover an AutoInvest transaction, the scheduled investment will be skipped, and you will receive a notification from Horizon Bank. Although the transaction will not be retried on that specific date, you have the option to manually invest by replenishing your account and placing an order through the Horizon App. Provided your AutoInvest configuration remains active, the system will automatically attempt to execute the investment again on the next scheduled date.\"}]}, {\"task_id\": \"task_2\", \"resolved_subquery\": \"What is the minimum weekly amount for recurring automatic investments in a Stocks account?\", \"approved_parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_4bd34aa4\", \"content\": \"Question: At Horizon Bank, what is the lowest investment threshold for purchasing securities?\\n\\nAnswer: With Horizon Bank, you have the flexibility to initiate your investment portfolio by buying stocks and ETFs with a minimum investment of just USD {{faq_4bd34aa4_001}}.\"}]}, {\"task_id\": \"task_3\", \"resolved_subquery\": \"Is there any fee for changing the investment schedule for a Stocks account?\", \"approved_parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_9a88fadb\", \"content\": \"Question: Is it possible to configure multiple automated investment plans for equities through Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, you have the flexibility to establish numerous automated investment schedules for your stock portfolio, including multiple plans for the same security with varying frequencies. Furthermore, you can modify or terminate these instructions at any time, with changes taking effect from the next scheduled investment date.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_b8e22edc\", \"content\": \"Question: How does Horizon Bank's fee structure work for investment transactions?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, we provide a competitive fee environment for our investors. Until December {{faq_b8e22edc_001}}, {{faq_b8e22edc_002}}, trading US stocks and ETFs is commission-free. After this period, a commission of {{faq_b8e22edc_003}} applies, with a minimum charge of USD {{faq_b8e22edc_004}} per trade. For UK UCITS ETFs, a commission rate of {{faq_b8e22edc_005}} is applicable, with a minimum fee of USD {{faq_b8e22edc_006}} per trade. Additionally, a {{faq_b8e22edc_007}} GST is levied on commissions, and your Trade Confirmation will also serve as your Tax Invoice. Notably, Horizon Bank does not impose platform, custody, settlement, or corporate action handling fees. For a detailed breakdown, please navigate to the Horizon App, select your Profile, and then access the Legal section to view the Stocks Fee Schedule.\"}]}]\n\n        Internal Response-Block-to-Task Map (not customer-facing):\n        [{\"block_id\": \"block_1\", \"task_id\": \"task_1\"}, {\"block_id\": \"block_2\", \"task_id\": \"task_2\"}, {\"block_id\": \"block_3\", \"task_id\": \"task_3\"}]\n\n        Intent Clarification Inputs (the only source for intent clarification):\n        []\n\n        Terminal Retrieval Clarification Evidence (permitted only for factual related-topic suggestions in terminal clarification):\n        []\n\n        Decline Inputs (the only source for a decline