nAI: The Horizon Experience Centre is located inside FairPrice Xtra in VivoCity at #B2-23. Our representatives can guide you on the Horizon App and basic banking tasks. The centre is open daily from 11am to 7pm (with reduced hours on Christmas Eve, New Year's Eve, and Chinese New Year’s Eve from 11am to 3pm) and is closed on the major public holidays. For account‑specific assistance, please use the in‑app chat or call +65 313-HORIZON.\nUser: For a Stocks account, how do recurring automatic investments work, including the minimum weekly amount and any fee for changing the investment schedule?\nAI: To set up AutoInvest for equities, open the Horizon App, go to Investments → Stocks, select Automatic investments, choose the stock or ETF, set your preferred schedule and start date (if not specified the next working day is used), and specify the amount and currency. The required amount will be deducted from your Horizon Savings account in Singapore Dollars, converted to US Dollars at the current exchange rate, and you will receive a notification one day before the scheduled investment. You may create multiple automated plans, and you can modify or terminate any plan at any time; changes take effect from the next scheduled investment date. If your Savings balance is insufficient, the investment is skipped, you are notified, and the system will attempt the investment again on the next scheduled date.\n\nThe lowest amount you can invest in a stock or ETF is USD 10.\n\nYou can modify or cancel any automated investment plan at any time, and the changes will apply from the next scheduled investment date. Trading US stocks and ETFs is commission‑free until December 31 (2026). After that date a commission of 0.05% applies with a minimum charge of USD 2.99 per trade. For UK UCITS ETFs the commission is 0.05% with a minimum of USD 4 per trade. A GST of 9% is added on commissions, and there are no platform, custody, settlement, or corporate‑action handling fees.\nUser: how can i apply a loan\nAI: You may qualify for the Instant Loan if you meet the following criteria:\nBe a current Horizon Bank client with a Horizon credit card and sufficient unused credit limit (for existing clients).\nBe a Singapore citizen, permanent resident, or foreign national with a valid work pass (for new applicants).\nBe aged between 21 and 65 years.\nHave an annual income of at least S$30,000 if you are a Singapore citizen or permanent resident.\nHave an annual income of at least S$60,000 if you are a foreigner holding a valid work pass.\nUser: i lost my card, how do i apply loan in app, where's your physical branch that i can visit?\n    User Baseline (advisory only; do not treat it as a current request): The customer knows Horizon Bank has no traditional branches; they can visit the Horizon Experience Centre at FairPrice Xtra VivoCity (unit B2-23) for in-person app guidance and general queries. Centre hours: daily 11 am‑7 pm, 11 am‑3 pm on Christmas Eve, New Year’s Eve, Chinese New Year’s Eve; closed on Christmas Day, New Year’s Day, Chinese New Year public holidays. Account-specific actions (personal detail updates, dispute resolution, voucher checks) must be done via in-app chat or by calling +65 313‑HORIZON. ATM locations can be found using the Horizon website locator; cash withdrawals are supported at Horizon-branded ATMs and Standard Chartered ATMs that accept Visa, both locally and abroad.\n    Current Graph Context: active_plan=False, retrieved_knowledge=False\n    Recalled Prior-Session Context Is Available: True\n    Latest User Input: \"i lost my card, how do i apply loan in app, where's your physical branch that i can visit?\"\n\n    STEP 1 — TRIAGE A BANKING REQUEST for the whole turn.\n    1. ESCALATION: User explicitly demands a human agent or manager.\n    2. CLARIFICATION: The input is PURELY chitchat, greetings, or completely unrelated to banking (e.g., \"Hello\", \"How are you\", \"What is the weather\").\n    3. VALID_REQUEST: Anything else — a banking-relevant question, follow-up, or request, even if part of it turns out to be non-compliant or off-topic once decomposed.\n\n    STEP 2 — ONLY when triage_status is VALID_REQUEST, decompose the LATEST USER INPUT into its distinct customer-request components. A component is one question, request, or independently answerable topic. Do not split one coherent question into artificial fragments; do not impose a numerical cap.\n    - Resolve pronouns, ellipsis, or short continuations (\"yes\", \"that one\", \"proceed\") into a standalone, self-contained rephrasing using the Recent Conversation Context.\n    - CONVERSATIONAL CONTINUATION: Produce ZERO components when the user is simply providing information requested in a previous step (e.g., \"I have MyInfo ready\", \"Next\", \"Proceed\") AND Current Graph Context confirms an active plan or retrieved knowledge exists. If recalled prior-session context is available but the current graph has neither an active plan nor retrieved knowledge, treat a continuation such as \"yes, continue\" as one new standalone component describing the recalled topic.\n\n    STEP 3 — For EACH component, assign a resolution:\n    - VALID: the component is financial/banking in nature AND does not, on its face, require Horizon to violate the MAS Compliance Context above.\n    - DECLINE: the component either (a) is NOT a financial/banking request at all — decline_reason_category=\"non_financial\" — or (b) would require Horizon to violate the MAS Compliance Context, e.g. personalized investment/trading advice, helping bypass KYC/AML checks, or other prohibited conduct — decline_reason_category=\"non_compliant\".\n\n    Do NOT judge whether Horizon offers the specific product or service — that is a separate, later step with its own matrix access. Only judge compliance and financial relevance here. When genuinely unsure whether a component is financial, prefer VALID and let the later step decide.\n\n    Output JSON ONLY:\n    {\"triage_status\":