{"timestamp": "2026-08-17T17:39:13.808+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_e5ffd6da-0007-4e69-8d1f-bb800fd708e2", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n        TASK-LEVEL SUFFICIENCY AND EVIDENCE SELECTION\n        You are a groundedness auditor for a read-only Horizon Bank FAQ assistant.\n        Evaluate EACH supplied task independently. A parent is sufficient only if it directly supports that task.\n\n        Original User Message (advisory context only; never use it as an\n        individual task's completeness target): what's the procedure of applying a loan\n        Trusted Conversation Context: Last Session Recall (advisory only; not current state):\nThe Horizon Experience Centre at FairPrice Xtra VivoCity (unit B2-23) offers in-person guidance on using the Horizon app, basic banking tasks, and general queries. It cannot handle account-specific actions (personal detail updates, dispute resolution, voucher checks). For those, use in-app chat or call +65 313-HORIZON. Hours: daily 11 am-7 pm, reduced to 11 am-3 pm on Christmas Eve, New Year’s Eve, Chinese New Year’s Eve; closed on Christmas Day, New Year’s Day, and Chinese New Year public holidays.\n\nCurrent-Session Rolling Context (advisory only):\nNone\n\nCurrent Session Trusted History (latest 10 turns):\nAI: Hello! I am Horizon. How can I assist you today?\nUser: What services are available at the Horizon Experience Centre?\nAI: The Horizon Experience Centre is located inside FairPrice Xtra in VivoCity at #B2-23. Our representatives can guide you on the Horizon App and basic banking tasks. The centre is open daily from 11am to 7pm (with reduced hours on Christmas Eve, New Year's Eve, and Chinese New Year’s Eve from 11am to 3pm) and is closed on the major public holidays. For account‑specific assistance, please use the in‑app chat or call +65 313-HORIZON.\nUser: For a Stocks account, how do recurring automatic investments work, including the minimum weekly amount and any fee for changing the investment schedule?\nAI: To set up AutoInvest for equities, open the Horizon App, go to Investments → Stocks, select Automatic investments, choose the stock or ETF, set your preferred schedule and start date (if not specified the next working day is used), and specify the amount and currency. The required amount will be deducted from your Horizon Savings account in Singapore Dollars, converted to US Dollars at the current exchange rate, and you will receive a notification one day before the scheduled investment. You may create multiple automated plans, and you can modify or terminate any plan at any time; changes take effect from the next scheduled investment date. If your Savings balance is insufficient, the investment is skipped, you are notified, and the system will attempt the investment again on the next scheduled date.\n\nThe lowest amount you can invest in a stock or ETF is USD 10.\n\nYou can modify or cancel any automated investment plan at any time, and the changes will apply from the next scheduled investment date. Trading US stocks and ETFs is commission‑free until December 31 (2026). After that date a commission of 0.05% applies with a minimum charge of USD 2.99 per trade. For UK UCITS ETFs the commission is 0.05% with a minimum of USD 4 per trade. A GST of 9% is added on commissions, and there are no platform, custody, settlement, or corporate‑action handling fees.\nUser: how can i apply a loan\nAI: You may qualify for the Instant Loan if you meet the following criteria:\nBe a current Horizon Bank client with a Horizon credit card and sufficient unused credit limit (for existing clients).\nBe a Singapore citizen, permanent resident, or foreign national with a valid work pass (for new applicants).\nBe aged between 21 and 65 years.\nHave an annual income of at least S$30,000 if you are a Singapore citizen or permanent resident.\nHave an annual income of at least S$60,000 if you are a foreigner holding a valid work pass.\nUser: i lost my card, how do i apply loan in app, where's your physical branch that i can visit?\nAI: Open the Horizon App, go to the card overview screen, tap \"View & Manage Card\", then select \"Freeze Card\" to temporarily disable the card.\n\nAfter freezing, stay in \"View & Manage Card\", tap \"Order Replacement\" to request a new card; the old card will be permanently deactivated.\n\nWhen you receive the new card, replace the old card number in any subscriptions or recurring payments.\n\n\n\nTo begin a balance transfer, open the Horizon App, tap the \"More\" option, then go to the \"Loan\" section and select \"Other Flexible Loans\" to start your application.\n\nThe Horizon Experience Centre is located within FairPrice Xtra in VivoCity at #B2-23. Representatives can help you navigate the Horizon App and answer general queries, but the centre is not a full bank branch; services such as updating personal details, resolving transaction disputes, or checking voucher redemption status cannot be done on‑site. For account‑specific assistance, use the in‑app chat or call +65 313-HORIZON. The centre is open daily from 11am to 7pm, with reduced hours on Christmas Eve, New Year's Eve, and Chinese New Year's Eve from 11am to 3pm, and closed on Christmas Day, New Year's Day, and Chinese New Year public holidays.\nUser: how do i apply for a stock\nAI: With Horizon Bank, you have the flexibility to initiate your investment portfolio by buying stocks and ETFs with a minimum investment of just USD 10.\nUser: what's the procedure of applying a loan\n        Task Inputs: [{\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"procedural\": \"procedure, applying, submission, onboarding\", \"policy\": \"requirements, criteria, eligibility, conditions\", \"conceptual\": \"loan, credit, application process, Horizon Bank\", \"target_commercial_product\": [\"Personal_Loan\", \"Credit_Card\"], \"target_intent\": [\"Application\", \"Eligibility\", \"General Inquiries\", \"Features And Limits\"], \"customer_component\": \"What is the procedure for applying for a loan with Horizon Bank?\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"procedure, applying, submission, onboarding\", \"policy\": \"requirements, criteria, eligibility, conditions\", \"conceptual\": \"loan, credit, application process, Horizon Bank\"}, {\"group_id\": \"retry_2\", \"procedural\": \"steps, walkthrough, guide, instruction\", \"policy\": \"prerequisites, documents, terms, conditions\", \"conceptual\": \"loan application, onboarding steps, credit request\"}]}, \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_85dbaadf\", \"content\": \"Question: What documentation is required to initiate a Horizon Bank credit card application?\\n\\nAnswer: To streamline your credit card application with Horizon Bank, Singaporean citizens and permanent residents can utilize MyInfo for expedited form completion. For foreign applicants, please ensure you have your passport and most recent payslip readily available for upload or photo capture via the Horizon App, in addition to accessing MyInfo.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_b3c9ded6\", \"content\": \"Question: What are the requirements for applying for a Horizon Bank credit card?\\n\\nAnswer: To be considered for a Horizon Bank credit card, you must meet specific criteria. If you are a Singaporean citizen or permanent resident between the ages of {{faq_b3c9ded6_001}} and {{faq_b3c9ded6_002}}, you will need to have an annual income of at least {{faq_b3c9ded6_003}}. For foreigners with a valid work pass, the requirement is an annual income of {{faq_b3c9ded6_004}}. Alternatively, if you are above {{faq_b3c9ded6_005}} years old, the annual income requirements are {{faq_b3c9ded6_006}} for Singaporean citizens or permanent residents, and {{faq_b3c9ded6_007}} for foreigners with a valid work pass.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_d5c931d4\", \"content\": \"Question: What steps do I need to take to enroll in Horizon Bank's Visa Instalment program for my purchases?\\n\\nAnswer: To apply for Horizon Bank's Visa Instalment program, follow these steps: \\n   - When shopping online with participating merchants, identify the 'Instalments enabled by Visa' logo at checkout. Enter your Horizon card details, and available instalment plans will be presented. Choose your preferred plan and finalize your payment.\\n   - For in-store purchases, after tapping your card to pay, you will be shown the available instalment plans. Select the one that suits you best and complete the transaction. \\n   Upon successful enrolment, you will receive a notification through the Horizon App. Please note that the minimum transaction amount to qualify for this program is {{faq_d5c931d4_001}}. Only primary Horizon credit cards are eligible, and if you have a linked card, ensure it is paired with your main credit card account. Debit cards and supplementary credit cards are not eligible for instalment plans and will be charged the full amount upfront.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_1542142e\", \"content\": \"Question: What types of Horizon Bank cards qualify for the Visa Instalments program offered by Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: To be eligible for the Visa Instalments program through Horizon Bank, you must have a primary Horizon Bank credit card. If you're using a Horizon Link card, it's essential that it's connected to your main credit card account. Please note that debit cards and any supplementary credit cards will not be part of an instalment plan and will instead be charged the full amount of the transaction immediately.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - A task is SUFFICIENT when its candidate parents directly answer its\n          own `customer_component`, even when another task from the same\n     