ent:\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_004}}. Log into the Horizon App.\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_005}}. Open the card dashboard and choose \\\"View & Manage Card.\\\"\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_006}}. Tap \\\"Freeze Card\\\" followed by \\\"Order Replacement.\\\"\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_007}}. Horizon will issue a new card and permanently deactivate the old one.\\n- You may also wish to file a police report.\\n- The new card will arrive with a different card number; be sure to update any recurring payments (e.g., subscriptions) with the new details.\\n- For additional assistance, select \\\"Contact Us\\\" from the app menu.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_33f045af\", \"content\": \"Question: My Horizon card has been compromised due to physical damage. What steps should I take to obtain a new one from Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: To acquire a replacement card, follow these straightforward steps: \\n    * Access your Horizon App account \\n    * Navigate to the 'Card Management' section \\n    * Choose the 'Replace Current Card' option \\n    * Indicate that your card is damaged to complete the request\"}]}, {\"task_id\": \"task_2\", \"status\": \"SUFFICIENT\", \"reason\": \"The candidate parents provide exact instructions on how to request an Instant Loan within the Horizon App and outline the eligibility criteria and requirements.\", \"approved_parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_1946c44f\", \"content\": \"Question: What steps should I follow to request an Instant Loan from Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: - Open the Horizon App, go to the **Money** menu, and select **Loan** to initiate the process.\\n- If you are not yet a Horizon customer, first download the Horizon App, then navigate to **Product Selection** and choose **Instant Loan** to begin your application.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_0ae0bb51\", \"content\": \"Question: Do I qualify for Horizon Bank’s Instant Loan offering?\\n\\nAnswer: - **For current Horizon Bank clients:**\\n  * You need to possess a Horizon credit card and have adequate unused credit limit.\\n- **For new applicants:**\\n  * Singapore citizens, permanent residents, and foreign nationals are all permitted to apply for the Instant Loan.\\n  * Every submission will be subject to Horizon Bank’s credit‑worthiness assessment.\\n\\nYou may request a credit facility provided you satisfy the following criteria:\\n- You are aged between {{faq_0ae0bb51_001}} and {{faq_0ae0bb51_002}} years.\\n- Your annual income is at least {{faq_0ae0bb51_003}} if you are a Singapore citizen or permanent resident.\\n- Your annual income is at least {{faq_0ae0bb51_004}} if you are a foreigner holding a valid work pass.\"}]}, {\"task_id\": \"task_3\", \"status\": \"SUFFICIENT\", \"reason\": \"The parents detail ATM locations and mention accessing the full directory of branch locations via the ATM/Branch Locator on the Horizon website.\", \"approved_parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_768b41d9\", \"content\": \"Question: Where can I locate an ATM to take out cash?\\n\\nAnswer: - Horizon Bank cardholders may withdraw funds from any Horizon‑branded or Standard Chartered (SCB) ATM throughout Singapore, as well as from Visa‑compatible ATMs overseas.\\n- Horizon‑branded machines are situated at FairPrice Xtra Vivocity, unit B{{faq_768b41d9_001}}‑{{faq_768b41d9_002}}.\\n- SCB ATMs are available at Bedok Mall, Bugis Junction, Vivocity, Sixth Avenue, Clementi Mall, NEX Serangoon, Serangoon Garden, Marine Parade, Changi Business Park, Tampines, Marina Bay Financial Centre and Battery Road.\\n- A full list of locations can be accessed via the ATM/Branch Locator on the Horizon website.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_6d8abb4a\", \"content\": \"Question: Where are the ATMs I can use to withdraw cash with my Horizon account?\\n\\nAnswer: - You may obtain cash at any Horizon‑branded ATM or at Standard Chartered Bank (SCB) ATMs that accept Visa, both within the country and overseas.\\n- Horizon‑branded machines are situated at FairPrice Xtra Vivocity, unit B{{faq_6d8abb4a_001}}‑{{faq_6d8abb4a_002}}.\\n- SCB ATMs are available at Bedok Mall, Bugis Junction, Vivocity, Sixth Avenue, Clementi Mall, NEX Serangoon, Serangoon Garden, Marine Parade, Changi Business Park, Tampines, Marina Bay Financial Centre, and Battery Road.\\n- A full directory of ATM and branch locations can be accessed via the ATM/Branch Locator on the Horizon website.\"}]}]\n    Intent-level clarification tasks (unresolved user-derived components; no FAQ evidence): []\n    Declined components (out of scope for this planner; do not plan a presentation or UI slot for them — their explanation is added separately, outside any presentation type you choose here): []\n\n    DEEPER PRESENTATION PRINCIPLE:\n    Select the presentation that visualizes the mental model the customer needs at this moment. The customer's higher-level intent selects the experience; approved FAQ evidence limits every title, item, stage, and option within that experience.\n\n    Choose one presentation type for EACH answerable task:\n    - TEXT — use when the customer needs to understand an explanation, policy, factual answer, or comparison. For a comparison, organise the supported facts into clear labelled sections; there is no dedicated comparison table yet.\n    - LIST — use when the customer needs to scan or remember independent items. This is optimal for three or more eligibility criteria, required documents, prerequisites, fees, limits, or security checks.\n    - PROGRESS — use when the customer needs to know where they are in, or complete, a process. This is especially appropriate for an account-opening or application/onboarding request asking how to proceed, how to apply, or what steps remain.\n    - ESCALATION — use only when human assistance was explicitly requested or required.\n\n    Rules:\n    - Never invent facts, parent IDs, or a banking action.\n    - Select evidence_parent_ids only from approved parents of the same task.\n    - A PROGRESS presentation is allowed only when the evidence supports at least two genuine